  "status": "published",
  "title": "Simple Wooden Chair",
  "summary": "A sturdy dining chair from 2x2 and 1x4 pine, joined with pocket screws and glue. A good first furniture build: straight cuts only, no lathe or router.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 6,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Cut the 2x2 boards into four legs (17 1/2 in), and the 1x4 boards into seat rails, a back rest and seat slats.",
    "Drill pocket holes on both ends of every rail with the pocket hole jig.",
    "Glue and screw the side rails to the legs to make two side frames; clamp until the glue grabs.",
    "Join the side frames with the front and back rails, checking the frame is square.",
    "Screw the seat slats on from below and fit the back rest between the rear legs.",
    "Sand from 80 to 220 grit, wipe off the dust, and apply two coats of polyurethane."
  ],
